# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# Verified 2026-10-08 on this project's *.pages.dev host: rules in this file ARE
# honoured there (a probe rule returned `301` with `Location` preserving the
# path via `:splat`), so the temporary host can 301 to a real domain later
# without any link going dead.
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#   - redirects are always followed, whether or not a static asset matches
#   - not applied to requests served by Pages Functions (this site has none)
#   - `*` wildcards; `:splat` carries the matched path into the destination
#
# When a real domain replaces the temporary one, this is the rule to ship:
#
# /*  https://example.com/:splat  301
#
# Add explicit rules for extension paths (/rss.xml, /robots.txt, /fonts/*,
# /sitemap-*.xml) and re-run the probe before announcing the switch.
